   "answer": "Random-Resample reduces cost by 96% but should not be interpreted as higher efficiency because variance-weighted selection concentrates the evaluation budget on long-running, multi-turn tasks where candidate harnesses show different success and failure outcomes, whereas uniform sampling also spends its budget on easier tasks that terminate quickly [3:25]. Under the same 20% evaluation budget, Random-Resample achieves a final performance 3.3 points lower than Task-CoEvolve, indicating that the cost reduction does not reflect better optimization efficiency [3:25]."
